  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nCentral idea: We will search for a step function `h` that minimizes the maximum overlap `C5` by exploring solutions at multiple grid resolutions (n_points). This reduces the risk of getting stuck in local optima. For each resolution, we use a local optimization approach with delayed-gradient updates to maintain budget efficiency. The algorithm will explore 3-4 resolution levels, escalating when the budget allows, to gradually refine the solution.\n\nKey improvements:\n- Multi-resolution exploration balances breadth (lower n_points) and depth (higher n_points)\n- Modified local optimization shifts gradient updates judiciously to save computations\n- Cache reuse avoids redundant calculations across steps\n- uses exact but delayed gradient updates to prioritize objective improvement\n\nBottleneck addressed:\nDirect continuous optimization is too prone to local optima. Our delayed-gradient approach allows skipping convergence checks when possible, cutting iteration counts.\n\nLimitations:\n- Resolves only within uniform grids\n- Cross-grid interpolation could be more sophisticated\n- Gradient approximation may drift, but we accept it for budget reasons\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nRepresentation: `h` as a vector of length `n_points` in `\u211d_0^1`\nObjective: min_c5(h) = max_{k\u2208Z}(\u222b_{x=0}^{2}h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx)\nApproximation: \n    corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n    C5 = (corr.max()) * dx   (dx=2/n_points)\n\nConstraints:\n    \u2211_{i} h[i] * dx = 1 (equivalent to \u2211h[i] = n_points/2)\n\nThe solution will be represented by:\n    h_values: vector of length n_points (after scaling to satisfy constraints)\n    c5_value: float\n    n_points: chosen integer\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nPre-initialization:\n    - Compute initial h at 80 points (down-sampled from parent)\n    - Define resolution hierarchy: [80, 240, (optional 320)]\n    - Set time budget per resolution level\n\nLevel 1 (80 points):\n    - Initial samples: from parent or uniform random search\n    - Use delayed-gradient optimization (gradient when feasible, numerical otherwise)\n    - Initial step: simplex method (NLopt)\n\nLevel 2 (240 points):\n    - Two-stage process:\n        * Stage A: Efficient grid interpolation (preserve integrals)\n        * Stage B: Iterative refinement with bounded gradient updates\n\nProgression rules:\n    - Move to next resolution if C5 improves by \u22652% AND budget \u226530% complete\n    - Unless stuck in plateau\n\nCache maintenance:\n    - All cached vectors are normalized via projection to maintain constraints\n    - Projection Formula (solve for \u03b1):\n        Set h_new[i] = clip(h_old[i], 0,1)\n        \u03b1 = (n_points/2) / sum(h_new)\n        h_scaled = \u03b1 * h_new\n\nTermination:\n    - Budget exhaustion or objective below 0.38\n    - Evaluate candidates via exact parent's methods\n\n4. Search choices and variations\nHierarchy resolution orders:\n    [80, 240, 320] \u2192 \n    Fix interval: 15 at each level per trial\n    Expected runtime: ~600s per trial\n\nGradient management policy:\n    - Period 1: No gradient (\u221e budget)\n    - Period 2: Every 5 iterations (10 evals)\n    - Whence: center of minima is safely established\n\nAdaptive step size:\n    n=80: initial step=auto\n    later levels: step proportional to 1.2^n (riskier moves)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nDominant costs: 2*n_points-1 correlation calls per iteration\nAllocation (example):\n    n=80: 300s\n    n=240: 600s\n    n=320: 400s\nMonitoring: Check completion fraction before initiating any resolution jump\n\nFallback strategy:\n    return vector from previously best candidate with minimal C5 (if >low bound)\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Validate: 0\u2264every value\u22641, integral within 1e-3 of n_points/2\n- Re-evaluate C5 via parent's method\n- Sanitizers: \n    - Check correlation lengths are finite\n    - Regression check: with n=80, expect around 0.4 values\n- Return sorted list of trial outcomes for record-keeping\n\nEnsure compatibility:\n    - Handles missing parent via uniform initialization\n    - n_points allowed: automatically detect operation parameters",
